:"We will use change the rafius to give components a softer, more modern look, a dashed style for borders with bigger line width.","type":"text"}]}],"chapter":"Borders","image":"ic_component_intro.png","projectFiles":"OUDS-Lime-Tutorial.zip","title":"Borders","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10,"backgroundImage":"ic_component_intro.png","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","kind":"hero"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"caption":[],"code":"tutorial-lime-4.swift","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Now let’s add the border provider with tokens overrides. We will override ","type":"text"},{"code":"radiusMedium","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"styleDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"widthThin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to make components different.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"media":null,"runtimePreview":"tutorial-lime-4.png","type":"step"}],"anchor":"Overriding-border-tokens","title":"Overriding border tokens","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","kind":"contentAndMedia","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Border tokens are defined in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrangeThemeBorderSemanticTokensProvider"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","assessments":[{"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Are border semantic tokens isolated?"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","content":[],"choices":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No, plenty of components used border semantic tokens"}]}],"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Border semantic tokens are semantic tokens, so they define high level source of truth used by components."}]}],"isCorrect":true},{"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The aim of semantic tokens is to be used by higher level tokens, e.g. for components","type":"text"}]}],"isCorre